1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,700
I'm Pluto;

2
00:00:00,750 --> 00:00:02,200
I built ExitPlan alone.

3
00:00:02,250 --> 00:00:04,075
This is my own hedge:

4
00:00:04,125 --> 00:00:09,700
two SOL in my wallet, two SOL short on Hyperliquid, a hundred dollars in Kamino.

5
00:00:09,750 --> 00:00:13,075
I need three hundred dollars out without breaking it.

6
00:00:13,125 --> 00:00:14,575
Here's what ExitPlan checks.

7
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:22,587
Hyperliquid's withdrawable is not equity minus maintenance margin.

8
00:01:22,637 --> 00:01:31,488
I reserve margin with the exchange's transfer rule, the larger of initial margin and 10% of notional per position, and check it against the exchange's own withdrawable.

9
00:01:31,538 --> 00:01:36,434
Unified accounts keep the equity in the spot USDC balance, so I read that too.

10
00:01:36,484 --> 00:01:39,071
A route the exchange would reject is worthless.

11
00:01:39,121 --> 00:01:50,939
Reductions are sized in the 0.01 SOL lot from `meta`, priced at your `userFees` taker rate, checked against the $10 minimum, and the rehearsal walks `l2Book` to build the inner order in the exchange's wire shape.

12
00:01:50,989 --> 00:01:57,532
The sell leg is the real Jupiter swap, built for your wallet and run through `simulateTransaction` with signature verification off.

13
00:01:57,582 --> 00:02:07,093
The Kamino leg is the real withdraw instruction set, simulated the same way, and I read the USDC token account out of the simulation to report what would arrive.

14
00:02:07,143 --> 00:02:08,082
Read-only by design:

15
00:02:08,132 --> 00:02:12,038
the first version must be right before it is allowed to act.

16
00:02:12,088 --> 00:02:13,686
Integer-cent arithmetic and fail-closed validation:

17
00:02:13,736 --> 00:02:16,983
a bad or stale input stops planning instead of guessing.

18
00:02:17,033 --> 00:02:19,950
Every number carries its evidence label, scenario or imported.

19
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:22,575
the engine and the report are modules;

20
00:02:22,625 --> 00:02:26,325
a bot or a CI job can run the pre-flight.

21
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:42,575
Next is execution behind the same check:

22
00:02:42,625 --> 00:02:48,950
Phantom signs the Solana legs, a Hyperliquid builder code routes the short, CCTP brings the USDC home.

23
00:02:49,000 --> 00:02:51,200
Today nothing is signed or sent.
